{
  "_comment": [
    "Date-stamped price sheet for claude-code-cli-cost-tracker.",
    "Units: USD per 1,000,000 tokens. Two sources, each verified on its date:",

    "  • Ollama Cloud rows (off_peak: true) — transcribed from",
    "    ollama.com/pricing on the as_of date. Their 'cached input' rate is",
    "    stored as cache_read. Ollama publishes no separate cache-write",
    "    rate, so writes bill at the input rate (both TTLs). Rows tagged",
    "    off_peak bill at half the listed rate when the analyzer runs with",
    "    --off-peak — a blanket half rate over the entire selection (no",
    "    per-turn time-window check).",
    "    Rows whose cached-input rate is unpublished on Ollama's page ('–':",
    "    nemotron-3-nano, mistral-large-3) use their input rate — an",
    "    understatement, never a spike.",
    "    Not priced: 'clef' (no published output/cached rate -> $0) and",
    "    qwen3-coder (absent from Ollama's table) — turns on unpriced",
    "    models are counted, billed $0, and named in the output.",
    "    Ollama plans (Pro/Max/Team) spend monthly usage credits at these",
    "    token rates, so figures track credits consumed, not cash.",

    "  • Claude rows — first-party Anthropic API list rates (model table",
    "    verified 2026-10-06). Writes use the standard multipliers: 5m =",
    "    1.25x input, 1h = 2.0x input. cache_read is per-model as",
    "    published — no longer uniformly 0.1x input (Fable 5.1 $0.25,",
    "    Opus 5.5 $0.20, Sonnet 5.5 $0.20).",
    "    claude-mythos-5-1 is Project Glasswing only.",
    "    claude-haiku-5-5 is tiered: shown rates are up-to-100K; beyond",
    "    that it bills $0.50 input / $2.50 output, so big-prompt turns are",
    "    under-priced by this sheet.",
    "    Claude fast mode (Opus 5 / 5.5, 2x rates) is not auto-detected",
    "    per turn; add rows manually if you need it.",
    "    Under a Claude subscription plan these figures are 'equivalent",
    "    API cost', not money billed.",

    "aliases map transcript model strings to sheet keys. resolve() also",
    "strips '[1m]'-style context-window suffixes and Ollama ':cloud' tags.",
    "To reprice history against other rates: copy this file, edit it, and",
    "pass --prices to the analyzer."
  ],

